# Keep the Airflow image build context lean and reproducible (Phase 8b). data/ is
# gitignored working output — the container generates its own; never bake a stale
# tiny.duckdb. The venv, caches and VCS metadata are irrelevant to the image.
#
# NOTE (round 2 #18): `docker compose down -v` removes containers/volumes but NOT
# the image. If a secret ever slipped in, `.dockerignore` is the defence AND
# `docker image rm otr-airflow-8b:latest` (or `docker compose … down --rmi local`)
# is the recovery — the layer must be dropped, not just the container.
.git
data
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
dbt/target
dbt/logs
logs
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.claude
# Terraform provider cache (~100 MB) and any future backend state (round 2 #2).
**/.terraform
**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Secrets must never be baked by `COPY . /opt/otr` (review rounds 1–2, #7/#1).
# Docker's matcher (moby/patternmatcher — NOT Go's filepath.Match, which has no
# `**`) expands a leading `**/` to any depth INCLUDING the root, so one form
# catches infra/.env, infra/sa-key.json, orchestration/.env and ./.env alike.
# None are committed; the set is .gitignore's secrets block, `**/`-anchored —
# equal by construction (tests/test_infra.py::test_gitignore_and_dockerignore_secret_globs_agree).
# secrets:begin
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/*.p8
**/*-key.json
**/*-credentials.json
**/credentials*
**/service-account*.json
# secrets:end
